### Linked issue

Closes `byissue/issues/062-x-ff-restore-pi-codemode-nested-rows.md`

### Type of change

- [x] Bug fix
- [ ] New feature
- [ ] Enhancement
- [ ] Refactor
- [ ] Docs

### Reasoning

The daemon runs an agent's code-mode script as one tool call that spawns nested shell, read and search
calls. 484446b7a stopped those nested calls from streaming as their own rows, to quiet the transcript,
and gave the parent a collapsible summary badge instead. Both halves read wrong in use: collapsed, the
badge was the only thing on screen and it hid what the script actually did; expanded, the children sat
in the same column as the parent, so a glob plus a read plus a test run looked like three separate
top-level actions the agent took on its own.

This PR reverts the row suppression and fixes the presentational problem the revert exposes. The nested
calls stream as rows again, and the app buckets them under their parent: the parent badge keeps its own
label and carries the child call counts as its secondary text, and the children render indented behind a
rail, always visible. The containment is legible at a glance without any interaction, which is what the
user needs from a transcript they are monitoring from a phone.

### Goals

- Nested tool calls inside a code-mode script stream as their own rows again, so nothing is lost from the
  transcript and nothing has to be expanded to be seen.
- The app shows the parent and its children as one unit: parent badge reads `Codemode  ran 1 command, read
  1 file, and searched 1 time`, children sit indented behind a vertical rail.
- The parent row still degrades to a readable summary on reload, where the nested rows are gone from the
  stored transcript: the replay path rebuilds the summary from `metadata.nestedSummary` on the parent's
  tool result.
- The mock load-test agent emits a code-mode call with nested children, so the layout can be reviewed
  without a provider key.

### Non-goals

- No protocol change. `parentToolCallId` and `nestedSummary` ride in the tool call's open `metadata`
  record (`packages/protocol/src/messages.ts`), which is tagged `COMPAT(piNestedToolCalls)` on the
  server side.
- No new interaction. Nested groups have no expand/collapse state at all; `expandedToolCallGroupIds`
  still serves only the top-level overview groups, whose existing testIDs are untouched.
- Child rows are not persisted as their own transcript entries on the reload path. Restoring them would
  mean writing nested ids into the canonical timeline; the parent summary covers that case for now.

### QA

Automated, and the visual claim is asserted rather than eyeballed:

- New e2e `packages/app/e2e/browser/nested-codemode-rows.spec.ts` drives the mock provider and asserts
  the transcript itself — the parent badge is visible and contains `ran 1 command`, `npx vitest run
  --bail=1` and `nested-codemode.ts` rows are visible with nothing clicked, and the child row's x is at
  least 16px right of the parent's. It screenshots the region as an artifact. 1 passed.
- `packages/app/e2e/browser/tool-call-overview-sheet.spec.ts` (2 cases) and `tool-call-shimmer.spec.ts`
  (1 case) still pass alongside it: 4 passed total in one run, browser project. This is the check that
  the new nested rendering did not disturb the top-level overview groups it shares `ExpandableBadge`
  and the summary formatter with.
- `packages/app/src/tool-calls/detail-level/overview/summary.test.ts` 4 cases (empty summary, singular vs
  plural, serial comma, capitalization) and `nested-codemode.test.ts` 6 cases pass.
- Server side: `packages/server/src/server/agent/providers/pi/agent.test.ts` 97 passed (nested rows carry
  `parentToolCallId`), `history-mapper.test.ts` 6 passed (nestedCalls to nestedSummary on replay),
  `mock-load-test-agent.test.ts` 18 passed. The real pi e2e case asserting the nested row reaches the
  canonical timeline passed with `PI_REAL_TEST_MODEL=bytetrueapi/deepseek-flash`.
- `npm run typecheck` (six workspaces), `npm run lint` (3383 files, 0 warnings) and `npm run
  format:check` clean.

Observed on web, the only platform this app builds for. The transcript reads: `Edit
packages/app/src/hooks/use-scroll-anchor.ts`, `Shell node scripts/simulate-stream-burst.mjs`, then
`Codemode  ran 1 command, read 1 file, and searched 1 time` with the three nested rows indented under it.

